  "description": "This circular walk explores the area around the Bedfordshire village of Harlington. The route visits two of the major walking highlights of the area at Sharpenhoe Clappers and Sundon Hills Country Park. It's a varied walk with woodland trails, countryside paths and hill climbs with splendid views of the surrounding Chiltern Hills from the high points. You can start the walk from Harlington rail station which is served by Thameslink route trains. Trains run to Harlington from Flitwick, Bedford, Luton, Luton Airport Parkway, Harpenden, St Albans, Central London, East Croydon, Gatwick Airport and Brighton.",
